sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client
    participant Appointment as Appointment Service
    participant Patient as Patient Service
    participant Availability as Availability Service
    participant Notification as Notification Service

    Client->>Appointment: POST /api/appointments + Idempotency-Key
    alt Existing key and matching fingerprint
        Appointment->>Appointment: Load persisted appointment
        Appointment-->>Client: 200 OK with replayed booking response
    else Existing key and different fingerprint
        Appointment-->>Client: 409 Conflict
    else New key
        Appointment->>Patient: GET /api/patients/{id}/eligibility
        Patient-->>Appointment: Eligibility result
        Appointment->>Availability: POST /api/v1/slots/{id}/reservations
        Availability->>Availability: Conditional capacity update and reservation insert
        Availability-->>Appointment: Reservation ID
        Appointment->>Appointment: Persist appointment and unique idempotency key
        alt Appointment persistence fails
            Appointment->>Availability: POST /api/v1/reservations/{id}/release
            Availability-->>Appointment: Reservation release result
            Appointment-->>Client: Error response
        else Appointment persisted
            loop Bounded transient retries
                Appointment->>Notification: POST /api/notifications
                alt Event accepted or duplicate replayed
                    Notification->>Notification: Persist or load unique appointment event
                    Notification-->>Appointment: 202 ACCEPTED response
                else Transient failure or timeout
                    Notification-->>Appointment: Failure / no response
                end
            end
            Appointment->>Appointment: Store notification status and attempt count
            Appointment-->>Client: 201 Created with booking and notification status
        end
    end
